{
  "chapter.3F42AE98B7586A25.title": "07 • Super Factory Manager: Program a Factory",
  "task.694CCD813BB87480.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.4EF7F4D3881BB980.title": "Start here: Super Factory Manager",
  "quest.4EF7F4D3881BB980.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.4EF7F4D3881BB980.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Super Factory Manager moves items and other resources through a cable network according to a readable program. Labels describe inventories, and timed rules decide what moves, where it goes and how much stays behind. It is especially useful when one complicated production line would otherwise need many filters.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Your route: manager and labels -> a two-chest transfer -> filters and limits -> a furnace line -> diagnostics and a maintainable factory.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Read the next guide card before building. This chapter teaches working setups; it does not replace JEI recipes or the mod's own manual."
  ],
  "task.76DC6B9ABE38FD5F.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.4A7B300A42FB222F.title": "How to use this guide",
  "quest.4A7B300A42FB222F.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.4A7B300A42FB222F.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Arrows suggest a learning order. Item tasks check what you carry; a checkmark is your own confirmation of a practical step. Neither is proof that an entire machine or colony works.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Open a quest, read Why / Do / Tip, then click its item to inspect it in JEI. R shows recipes and U shows uses with the default bindings. Read ahead, complete the described experiment, and only then tick practical tasks. Items are not consumed.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use JEI for this pack's quantities and substitutions. Pick a small test area and keep outputs visible. Existing equipment can count; briefly pick it up only when safe. Troubleshooting and a final project are at the end."
  ],
  "quest.50469B0A1FB3B1AD.title": "The manager and its program",
  "quest.50469B0A1FB3B1AD.quest_subtitle": "Item milestone",
  "quest.50469B0A1FB3B1AD.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Manager executes the program stored on a disk. Cables connect accessible inventories; the program supplies the transfer rules.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Make a Manager, Program Disk, Inventory Cable and Label Gun. Place the Manager near two ordinary chests and connect both with cable. Open its interface and locate the disk editor and examples.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Start with ordinary chests. Machine-side restrictions introduce a second problem before you have learned the language."
  ],
  "task.41430FDF43977C7C.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.1758CCC36719D7CB.title": "Name the endpoints",
  "quest.1758CCC36719D7CB.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.1758CCC36719D7CB.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A label is a name the program uses to select network endpoints. A typo or missing label can make correct-looking code select nothing.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Use the Label Gun controls shown in its tooltip to label one chest input and the other output. Apply/synchronize its labels to the Manager, then inspect the network to confirm both names.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use short, distinct names. When copying a setup, verify the Manager has the labels rather than assuming the gun alone configured it."
  ],
  "task.00D9A9E45A80EDD2.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.119971C8963166B4.title": "Your first working program",
  "quest.119971C8963166B4.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.119971C8963166B4.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A timed block repeatedly gathers candidate resources with INPUT and transfers them with OUTPUT. INPUT alone does not move items into a hidden buffer.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Put a few cobblestone in input. Enter the example below, save the disk and run it. Confirm the cobblestone appears in output, then stop the program and move it back.",
    "",
    "&b&lEXAMPLE&r",
    "NAME \"Two chest transfer\"",
    "EVERY 20 TICKS DO",
    "  INPUT FROM \"input\"",
    "  OUTPUT TO \"output\"",
    "END",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "20 ticks is about one second at normal server speed. An empty source or full destination is not necessarily a syntax error."
  ],
  "task.1B82C9393CD95E65.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.7D17FF2200A2F2B7.title": "Read errors before changing hardware",
  "quest.7D17FF2200A2F2B7.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.7D17FF2200A2F2B7.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The editor can catch malformed syntax, while execution diagnostics reveal rules that select nothing or cannot transfer.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the Manager's error/status display. Deliberately change input to an unused label, observe the result, then restore it. Compare that problem with a missing END in the editor.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Change one thing at a time. A successful parse only proves the language is valid; it cannot guarantee your chest contains the requested item."
  ],
  "task.58E2E64B957D326A.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.6D5CB633FA418D5C.title": "Filter by exact item",
  "quest.6D5CB633FA418D5C.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.6D5CB633FA418D5C.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Explicit identifiers prevent a broad transfer from emptying supplies that belong elsewhere.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Change the input line to INPUT minecraft:cobblestone FROM \"input\". Put cobblestone and dirt together in the source and verify only cobblestone moves.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use the actual registry identifier from advanced tooltips or the network inspector. Display names and translated item names are not identifiers."
  ],
  "task.4C245D9170C47BAD.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.660B3BD35352E197.title": "Keep a reserve",
  "quest.660B3BD35352E197.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.660B3BD35352E197.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Limits control the amount selected or delivered. A reserve prevents automation from taking every ingredient you need by hand.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Open the bundled limits example and compare INPUT 5 RETAIN 3 minecraft:cobblestone FROM \"input\" with your unrestricted rule. Test a source of ten cobblestone and observe several cycles.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "An input limit applies per execution, not forever. RETAIN protects a stock level; a transfer of five repeated every second can still drain the rest."
  ],
  "task.5BA2009093529903.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.70159CC525975883.title": "Separate unrelated jobs with FORGET",
  "quest.70159CC525975883.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.70159CC525975883.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Within a trigger, selected resources remain available to later statements. FORGET clears that selection before another independent transfer.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the bundled furnace_manager example and identify each FORGET between ingredients, fuel and results. Add a second independent transfer to your chest test, separated by FORGET.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "If a later output receives an unexpected earlier ingredient, inspect selection lifetime before adding more filters."
  ],
  "task.191D06CE07194226.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.3B2C8E2A3D6CB5F9.title": "Respect machine faces",
  "quest.3B2C8E2A3D6CB5F9.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.3B2C8E2A3D6CB5F9.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Many machines expose different inventory slots from different sides. A cable connection does not make every slot available from every direction.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Connect a vanilla furnace, an ore chest, a fuel chest and a result chest. Label them feed, fuel, furnace and results. Read the slots_and_sides example before attempting a transfer.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "For a vanilla furnace, top accepts smelting ingredients; bottom can extract results and accepts fuel through its exposed fuel slot. Modded machines may behave differently."
  ],
  "task.58B68DA4630CE865.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.5BAD5A0D9DCBBFAB.title": "Run a small furnace line",
  "quest.5BAD5A0D9DCBBFAB.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.5BAD5A0D9DCBBFAB.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "This program maintains a small ingredient buffer, supplies fuel and removes results without mixing the three jobs.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Use the program below with the labels from the previous step. Add a few raw iron and coal, run it, then verify iron ingots reach results. Keep the output chest visible.",
    "",
    "&b&lEXAMPLE&r",
    "NAME \"Workshop furnace\"",
    "EVERY 20 TICKS DO",
    "  INPUT FROM feed",
    "  OUTPUT 8 TO EACH furnace TOP SIDE",
    "  FORGET",
    "  INPUT minecraft:coal FROM fuel",
    "  OUTPUT RETAIN 1 TO EACH furnace BOTTOM SIDE",
    "  FORGET",
    "  INPUT FROM furnace BOTTOM SIDE",
    "  OUTPUT TO results",
    "END",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use plain coal for the first experiment. Fuel-container leftovers such as buckets deserve a separate tested rule."
  ],
  "task.12D7804E111DA741.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.715DE1057A2E5E50.title": "Scale to several machines",
  "quest.715DE1057A2E5E50.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.715DE1057A2E5E50.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A shared label can represent several machines. EACH changes whether a quantity applies separately to each endpoint.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Connect a second furnace under the same label. Compare distribution with the bundled limits and round_robin examples, then choose whether both furnaces should hold a small reserve or receive work in rotation.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not assume the first matching inventory is the only target. Inspect how many endpoints carry a shared label before using a large transfer."
  ],
  "task.2D8EDDF589B735C2.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.1BD6617C08FB567D.title": "Inspect the live network",
  "quest.1BD6617C08FB567D.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.1BD6617C08FB567D.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "The Network Tool reveals connections and endpoint details that are hard to see through walls or machine casings.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Inspect one working chest and one machine with the tool. Locate its inventory inspection controls in the tooltip, then compare exposed slots and resource types from two sides.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use this evidence to choose sides and identifiers. Guessing slot numbers from the GUI can fail because internal inventory numbering differs."
  ],
  "task.373EB43C3BA2CA81.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.2AD403F667C43882.title": "Tags and families of ingredients",
  "quest.2AD403F667C43882.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.2AD403F667C43882.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Tags let one rule match a compatible family such as a category of ingots. This is useful only if the receiving recipe accepts that family too.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the bundled tag_matching and filtering examples. Adapt one to a harmless chest sorting test, and verify both an intended match and an item that should stay behind.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "A broad tag can include valuable variants. Test with small quantities and inspect matches before connecting bulk storage."
  ],
  "task.5DF693BB81820B27.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.2100DDCF4B05190F.title": "Fluids are a separate resource type",
  "quest.2100DDCF4B05190F.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.2100DDCF4B05190F.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "SFM can move supported resources besides items. A fluid rule needs fluid endpoints and the fluid resource type; an item rule will not move the contents of a tank.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Connect two tanks and consult the bundled resource_types example. Test INPUT fluid::water FROM water_source followed by OUTPUT fluid:: TO water_destination inside a timed block.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Label the tanks exactly as written. Verify exposed tank faces and available destination capacity before increasing the amount."
  ],
  "task.250080817E1744FD.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.653C7C626AC9DC49.title": "Energy and other integrations",
  "quest.653C7C626AC9DC49.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.653C7C626AC9DC49.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Supported resource types depend on the installed integrations. The live example and inspector tell you what this build can access.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Open resource_types in the installed Manager and inspect its generated resource-type list. Choose an available energy integration and build a tiny source-to-buffer test using its exact syntax.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Copy the installed example's type name rather than guessing from a web tutorial for another SFM version. Keep power distribution independent from item-selection state."
  ],
  "task.25E6D026410784FC.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.51859F2558C202FC.title": "Pause on purpose",
  "quest.51859F2558C202FC.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.51859F2558C202FC.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A production line should be controllable when storage is full, ingredients are scarce or you want to work on the machine.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Read the bundled redstone_signals and if_statements examples. Add one simple condition or use the Manager's run control to stop your furnace line, and confirm it resumes cleanly.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Do not build a complicated condition until the unconditional transfer works. A stopped trigger and a failed transfer require different fixes."
  ],
  "task.56ECCA65AF34D6E1.title": "I read and understood this guide",
  "quest.1606B6261DA0E892.title": "Troubleshoot in a fixed order",
  "quest.1606B6261DA0E892.quest_subtitle": "Guide and tips",
  "quest.1606B6261DA0E892.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "Most silent failures come from labels, resource matching, exposed sides or destination capacity.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Check parse status, trigger timing, endpoint labels, source contents, filters, side/slot access and output space in that order. Temporarily reduce the line to one input and one output to isolate the fault.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Keep a working copy of your program outside the disk before major edits. Comments and descriptive labels save more time than clever compressed code."
  ],
  "task.65E732D8D478A9FF.title": "I completed the practical steps",
  "quest.77E937AE6C85076E.title": "Project: a readable processing cell",
  "quest.77E937AE6C85076E.quest_subtitle": "Practical checklist",
  "quest.77E937AE6C85076E.quest_desc": [
    "&6&lWHY&r",
    "A good SFM program is a small operating manual for your factory, not just a transfer that happened to work once.",
    "",
    "&a&lDO&r",
    "Run two furnaces with filtered input, retained fuel and a separate output. Demonstrate empty input, full output and restart behavior, then add comments explaining each block and save a backup copy.",
    "",
    "&e&lTIP&r",
    "Use slower triggers for ordinary storage work. Increase frequency only when observation shows the transfer interval is the actual bottleneck."
  ]
}
